Hi Joe,<br />
<br />
<span style="font-family:calibri,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11.0pt;">It was great talking to you. &nbsp;Battle of the Badges is a program we&rsquo;ve run across the country but are just starting to do it in this area.&nbsp; You can see a couple of articles online from other jurisdictions </span></span><a href="http://wjhl.com/2017/09/05/american-red-cross-news-channel-11s-annual-battle-of-the-badges-kicks-off/"><span style="font-family:calibri,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11.0pt;">here</span></span></a><span style="font-family:calibri,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11.0pt;">, </span></span><a href="http://ksnt.com/2017/05/09/topeka-first-responders-partner-with-red-cross-for-battle-of-the-badges-blood-drive/"><span style="font-family:calibri,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11.0pt;">here</span></span></a><span style="font-family:calibri,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11.0pt;">, and </span></span><a href="https://patch.com/massachusetts/worcester/american-red-cross-host-battle-badges-blood-drive"><span style="font-family:calibri,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11.0pt;">here</span></span></a><span style="font-family:calibri,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11.0pt;">.&nbsp; </span></span><br />
&nbsp;<br />
The basic idea is that different 911 branches challenge each other to&nbsp;see who can recruit the most donors to come to a blood drive.&nbsp;<br />
Every donor will be asked which branch they are donating for (i.e. voting for).&nbsp; At the end we&rsquo;ll give the winner a trophy. &nbsp;If you do it during May and June we should be able to supply T-Shirts.<br />
<br />
<span style="font-family:calibri,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11.0pt;">I&rsquo;ve attached a short flier on the program. &nbsp;Please let me know how I can help moving forward. &nbsp;If you can set a meeting, I&#39;d be more than willing to attend. &nbsp;</span></span><br />
&nbsp;<br />
<span style="font-family:calibri,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11.0pt;">Please let me know how I can help! &nbsp;</span></span><br />
